# STIG AS24-U2-000390: Only authenticated system administrators or the designated P
# STIG ID: V-214287 (MEDIUM)

META
    esp_id `apache-as24-u2-000390-ssl-key-perms-site-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `apache`
    criticality `high`

    title `STIG AS24-U2-000390: Only authenticated system administrators or the designated PKI Sponsor for the A`
    description `Only authenticated system administrators or the designated PKI Sponsor for the Apache web server must have access to the Apache web servers private key.`
    author `example-security`
    tags `apache,stig,disa-stig,combined`

    control_mapping `DISA-STIG:AS24-U2-000390,NIST-800-53:IA-5(2)(A)(1)`
    control_objective `IA-5(2)(A)(1)`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Apache:localhost:web-hardening`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Review and remediate per DISA Apache STIG guidance for AS24-U2-000390.`

    component_id `comp-apache-web`

    impl_IA_5_2_A_1 `This control is validated by checking the Apache HTTP server configuration against the DISA STIG baseline.`

META_END

DEF
    VAR config_path string `/etc/httpd/conf/httpd.conf`

    OBJECT module_check
        module `ssl_module`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE module_loaded
        loaded boolean = true
    STATE_END

    OBJECT httpd_config
        path VAR config_path
    OBJECT_END

    STATE directive_present
        content string contains `SSLCertificateKeyFile`
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN apache_module
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF module_loaded
            OBJECT_REF module_check
        CTN_END

        CTN file_content
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF directive_present
            OBJECT_REF httpd_config
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
